  data: {
    LLM: "Keep your low cards! In a 32-card deck, information is easy to track. If you have the 7 of Hearts, it is your most powerful defensive cardâ€”save it to 'under-play' any lead and force another player to take the point.\n\nKing of Hearts Protection: If you hold the King of Hearts, you MUST play specifically. If Hearts are led, play your King immediately if you think no one has the Ace. If you hold it until the end, you are almost guaranteed to take the -8 penalty.\n\nThe Lora Shedding: In the final round, prioritize playing your 'middle' cards (9s and 10s). These 'open' the board for your other cards, allowing you to empty your hand fast and secure the positive points needed for a comeback.",
    Player: "Keep your low cards! In a 32-card deck, information is easy to track. If you have the 7 of Hearts, it is your most powerful defensive cardâ€”save it to 'under-play' any lead and force another player to take the point.\n\nKing of Hearts Protection: If you hold the King of Hearts, you MUST play specifically. If Hearts are led, play your King immediately if you think no one has the Ace. If you hold it until the end, you are almost guaranteed to take the -8 penalty.\n\nThe Lora Shedding: In the final round, prioritize playing your 'middle' cards (9s and 10s). These 'open' the board for your other cards, allowing you to empty your hand fast and secure the positive points needed for a comeback.",
